# Install as /etc/joi-deploy.env. Read by deploy-joi.sh, nothing else.
#
# What *this box* runs, as opposed to what a generic install runs. It exists so
# that the deploy script on this machine can stay a byte-for-byte copy of the
# one in the repository: an edited copy is a fork, and a fork stops tracking the
# original without ever saying so.
#
# No secrets belong here. Provider keys are read by Core from /etc/joi-web.env
# and the system keyring; this file only decides which code and which characters
# a deploy picks up.
#
# Sourced by bash, so it is shell syntax. Every line uses `${VAR:-default}` so a
# deliberate one-off still wins:
#
#     JOI_BRANCH=some-branch joi-deploy

# The branch this box tracks. The script's own default is `main`, which is right
# for a generic install and wrong for a box running a feature branch -- naming it
# here is what keeps a plain `joi-deploy` correct. Getting this wrong no longer
# resets the checkout onto an unrunnable tree; verify_target.py refuses first.
JOI_BRANCH="${JOI_BRANCH:-main}"

# Which characters a visitor can meet. Every one of them is copied into the seed
# and served from this box, so this list is also the bandwidth bill: the sample
# VRM alone is 26MB per visitor who activates it.
JOI_CHARACTER_IDS="${JOI_CHARACTER_IDS:-momose-hiyori,test-tachie-catgirl}"
